The most common AI technology is **text mining**: software that reads documents and pulls out the facts. 12% of all Dutch firms used it in 2025, against 4% in 2023 ([CBS, 2025](https://www.cbs.nl/nl-nl/nieuws/2025/50/bedrijven-gebruiken-ai-vaakst-voor-marketing-of-verkoop)). Across OECD countries, too, most small firms buy AI ready-made rather than build it ([OECD, 2026](https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/empowering-smes-in-the-age-of-ai_bf5a9816-en.html)).

